ipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"O000175","fullName":"Rep. Ogles, Andrew [R-TN-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"F000480","fullName":"Rep. Fong, Vince [R-CA-20]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"Y000067","fullName":"Rep. Yakym, Rudy [R-IN-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"M001235","fullName":"Rep. Moore, Riley [R-WV-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-28","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WV"},{"bioguideId":"K000376","fullName":"Rep. Kelly, Mike [R-PA-16]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-23T14:44:40+00:00","id":"hjres89-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-02","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-12","text":"Became Public Law No: 119-17."},"laws":[{"number":"119-17","type":"Public Law"}],"number":"89","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Environmental Protection","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"O000019","district":23,"fullName":"Rep. Obernolte, Jay [R-CA-23]","party":"R","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-02","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This joint resolution nullifies the Environmental Protection Agency notice titled <em>California State Motor Vehicle and Engine and Nonroad Engine Pollution Control Standards; The ‘Omnibus’ Low NOX Regulation; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision</em> (90 Fed. Reg. 643) and published on January 6, 2025. Among other elements, the notice grants the California Air Resources Board request for a waiver for its Heavy-Duty Vehicle and Engine Omnibus Low NOX regulations. (Under the Clean Air Act, California may seek waivers of the preemption prohibiting states from enacting certain emission standards.)&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-04-25T00:59:09Z","versionCode":"00"},{"actionDate":"2025-06-12","actionDesc":"Public Law","text":"<p>This joint resolution revokes the waiver granted to the California Air Resources Board regarding new emissions standards for new 2024 and subsequent model year on-road heavy-duty&nbsp;vehicles and engines, off-road diesel engines, and off-road diesel-fueled auxiliary power units. (Under the Clean Air Act, California may seek waivers of the preemption prohibiting states from enacting certain emission standards.)</p><p>Specifically, the joint resolution nullifies the Environmental Protection Agency notice titled <a href=\"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/01/06/2024-31125/california-state-motor-vehicle-and-engine-and-nonroad-engine-pollution-control-standards-the-omnibus\">California State Motor Vehicle and Engine and&nbsp;Nonroad Engine Pollution Control Standards; The ‘Omnibus’ Low NOX Regulation; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision</a>.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-17T16:51:29Z","versionCode":"49"}],"title":"Providing congressional disapproval under chapter 8 of title 5, United States Code, of the rule submitted by the Environmental Protection Agency relating to \"California State Motor Vehicle and Engine and Nonroad Engine Pollution Control Standards; The 'Omnibus' Low NOX Regulation; Waiver of Preemption; Notice of Decision\".","type":"hjres","updateDate":"2026-09-22T19:08:23Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-23T03:03:30Z"}
